{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_pair.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.remote-pair\n     2\t  \"The pair channel of dao.stream.remote.md (3.3): a pair descriptor\n     3\t   names two remote descriptors, `:dao.stream.remote/in` and\n     4\t   `:dao.stream.remote/out`. `attach!` on it returns a channel whose\n     5\t   reader is a reflection of `in` and whose writer is a reflection of\n     6\t   `out` -- when a third peer serves both from its table, two peers\n     7\t   that cannot reach each other have a channel, and the third peer\n     8\t   runs nothing but mirror steps over two ring buffers, never\n     9\t   interpreting the requests and answers inside.\n    10\t\n    11\t   `attacher` is the composition's channel-end source for pair\n    12\t   descriptors, used the same way `dao.stream.remote/attacher` is:\n    13\t   `(attacher opts) -> attach!`, and `(attach! descriptor) -> result`\n    14\t   for a `:dao.stream/remote` descriptor whose `:dao.stream/channel`\n    15\t   is a pair descriptor.\n    16\t\n    17\t   **An `in` gap ends the channel** (3.3): the pair reader holds the\n    18\t   reading cursor on `in`'s reflection; when `next` there answers\n    19\t   `:dao.stream/gap`, frames were lost and which cannot be said, so\n    20\t   the reader answers `:dao.stream/end` from then on -- the gap is\n    21\t   never reported to an inner reader as a source's own gap. The outer\n    22\t   link then runs its ordinary channel-loss path (2.4): outstanding\n    23\t   ids are abandoned, each abandoned `append!` is reported\n    24\t   `append-unknown`, and reattachment is the caller's, by `attach!` on\n    25\t   the same pair descriptor, which mints a fresh reading cursor on\n    26\t   `in` at `:newest`.\"\n    27\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n    28\t            [dao.stream.remote :as remote]))\n    29\t\n    30\t\n    31\t;; =============================================================================\n    32\t;; The pair descriptor (3.3)\n    33\t;; =============================================================================\n    34\t\n    35\t(defn- pair-channel-descriptor?\n    36\t  \"True when `d` is a pair channel descriptor: it names two remote\n    37\t   descriptors, `:dao.stream.remote/in` and `:dao.stream.remote/out`.\"\n    38\t  [d]\n    39\t  (and (map? d)\n    40\t       (= :dao.stream/pair (:dao.stream/type d))\n    41\t       (map? (:dao.stream.remote/in d))\n    42\t       (map? (:dao.stream.remote/out d))))\n    43\t\n    44\t\n    45\t(defn- valid-pair-descriptor?\n    46\t  \"True when `d` is a `:dao.stream/remote` descriptor naming a pair\n    47\t   channel.\"\n    48\t  [d]\n    49\t  (and (stream/valid-descriptor? d)\n    50\t       (= :dao.stream/remote (:dao.stream/type d))\n    51\t       (pair-channel-descriptor? (:dao.stream/channel d))))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t;; =============================================================================\n    55\t;; The pair reader: in's gap translated to end (3.3)\n    56\t;; =============================================================================\n    57\t\n    58\t(defn- pair-reader\n    59\t  \"A channel reader over `in`, a reflection: every `cursor` mints\n    60\t   afresh on `in` at `:newest`, ignoring the anchor asked -- the pair\n    61\t   is a live channel, not a history browse, and a reattachment's fresh\n    62\t   cursor is the same mint this makes on first use. `next` follows\n    63\t   `in`'s own cursor, an internal position no caller threads back\n    64\t   here; an `in` gap or end marks the reader ended in `ended?`, shared\n    65\t   with the caller so a retired pair end can be told from a live one,\n    66\t   and every further read, forever, answers `:dao.stream/end` without\n    67\t   asking `in` again.\"\n    68\t  [in ended?]\n    69\t  (let [cursor (atom nil)\n    70\t        mint! (fn []\n    71\t                (let [r (stream/cursor in stream/anchor-newest)]\n    72\t                  (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n    73\t                    (reset! cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)))))]\n    74\t    (reify\n    75\t      stream/IDaoStreamReader\n    76\t\n    77\t      (cursor\n    78\t        [_ _anchor]\n    79\t        (if @ended?\n    80\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/end}\n    81\t          (do (mint!)\n    82\t              (if-some [c @cursor]\n    83\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok :dao.stream/cursor c}\n    84\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n    85\t                 :dao.stream/retry? true}))))\n    86\t\n    87\t      (next\n    88\t        [_ _c]\n    89\t        (if @ended?\n    90\t          {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/end}\n    91\t          (do (when-not @cursor (mint!))\n    92\t              (if-not @cursor\n    93\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error\n    94\t                 :dao.stream/retry? true}\n    95\t                (let [r (stream/next in @cursor)]\n    96\t                  (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n    97\t                    :dao.stream/ok\n    98\t                    (do (reset! cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r)) r)\n    99\t\n   100\t                    (:dao.stream/gap :dao.stream/end)\n   101\t                    (do (reset! ended? true)\n   102\t                        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/end})\n   103\t\n   104\t                    r))))))\n   105\t\n   106\t\n   107\t      stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   108\t\n   109\t      (close!\n   110\t        [_]\n   111\t        (reset! ended? true)\n   112\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok}))))\n   113\t\n   114\t\n   115\t;; =============================================================================\n   116\t;; The pair attacher\n   117\t;; =============================================================================\n   118\t\n   119\t(defn- build-pair-entry!\n   120\t  \"Attach `in` and `out` through `lower-attach!`, the composition's\n   121\t   attach entry for `:dao.stream/remote` descriptors, wrap them as one\n   122\t   channel end for `remote/attacher`'s `:dao.stream.remote/channels`,\n   123\t   and build the inner attacher scoped to that one entry. Neither\n   124\t   answering ok answers that attach's own failing result.\"\n   125\t  [lower-attach! pair-cd policy]\n   126\t  (let [in-r (lower-attach! (:dao.stream.remote/in pair-cd))]\n   127\t    (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome in-r))\n   128\t      in-r\n   129\t      (let [out-r (lower-attach! (:dao.stream.remote/out pair-cd))]\n   130\t        (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome out-r))\n   131\t          out-r\n   132\t          (let [ended? (atom false)\n   133\t                reader (pair-reader (:dao.stream/handle in-r) ended?)\n   134\t                out-h (:dao.stream/handle out-r)\n   135\t                inner (remote/attacher\n   136\t                        (merge policy\n   137\t                               {:dao.stream.remote/channels\n   138\t                                {pair-cd {:reader reader :writer out-h}}}))]\n   139\t            {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n   140\t             :ended? ended?\n   141\t             :inner inner}))))))\n   142\t\n   143\t\n   144\t(defn attacher\n   145\t  \"The pair channel's attach entry. `opts` carries\n   146\t   `:dao.stream.remote.pair/attach!`, the composition's attach entry\n   147\t   for `:dao.stream/remote` descriptors, used here to attach one\n   148\t   pair's `in` and `out`; `:dao.stream.remote/events`,\n   149\t   `:dao.stream.remote/resend-after` and `:dao.stream.remote/budget`\n   150\t   pass through as the served identity's own link policy, exactly as\n   151\t   `dao.stream.remote/attacher` takes them. One pair channel end is\n   152\t   built per distinct pair descriptor value and shared by every\n   153\t   identity attached through it -- `dao.stream.remote/attacher`'s own\n   154\t   one-link-per-channel-descriptor sharing, here for a channel this\n   155\t   namespace builds instead of one the composition wires statically.\n   156\t   Once a pair's `in` gaps the built end is retired; the next attach!\n   157\t   on the same pair descriptor value builds a fresh one, `in`'s cursor\n   158\t   minted afresh at `:newest` -- attach! on the same pair descriptor\n   159\t   resumes.\"\n   160\t  [opts]\n   161\t  (let [lower-attach! (:dao.stream.remote.pair/attach! opts)\n   162\t        policy (select-keys opts [:dao.stream.remote/events\n   163\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/resend-after\n   164\t                                  :dao.stream.remote/budget])\n   165\t        pairs (atom {})]\n   166\t    (fn [descriptor]\n   167\t      (if-not (valid-pair-descriptor? descriptor)\n   168\t        {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-descriptor}\n   169\t        (let [pair-cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)\n   170\t              cached (get @pairs pair-cd)]\n   171\t          (if (and cached (not @(:ended? cached)))\n   172\t            ((:inner cached) descriptor)\n   173\t            (let [built (build-pair-entry! lower-attach! pair-cd policy)]\n   174\t              (if-not (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome built))\n   175\t                built\n   176\t                (do (swap! pairs assoc pair-cd built)\n   177\t                    ((:inner built) descriptor))))))))))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
