{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/remote_meet.cljc'","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.remote-meet\n     2\t  \"The meeting board convention of dao.stream.remote.md (section 4):\n     3\t   none of this has a frame -- M is peers using sections 2 and 3, a\n     4\t   request and response service (section 5) over two ordinary table\n     5\t   entries.\n     6\t\n     7\t   M serves `:meet-requests`, surface `#{:writer}`, and `:meet-board`,\n     8\t   surface `#{:reader}`. A peer appends `{:meet/here <name>}` over a\n     9\t   channel whose attachment identity is its own reflexive address\n    10\t   (UDP) or a stand-in the composition supplies for any other channel;\n    11\t   M's interpreter answers with a `:meet/seen` posting on the board\n    12\t   naming the address it observed, never one a payload claimed. A\n    13\t   peer appends `{:meet/pair <name>}` to ask for a relay pair; M\n    14\t   creates two ring buffers, enters them in its table under a lease\n    15\t   (docs/design/dao.lease.md: the two identities are the subject, the\n    16\t   requesting peer the holder), and posts their descriptors, from the\n    17\t   asker's own side, on the board -- the asked-for peer mirrors `in`\n    18\t   and `out` to build its own pair descriptor over the same two\n    19\t   buffers (`dao.stream.remote-pair`).\n    20\t\n    21\t   `reflexive-tag` and `bound-gate` are the two middlewares\n    22\t   `:meet-requests`' table entry wraps: the first stamps every\n    23\t   append! with the channel attachment identity it arrived on, under\n    24\t   `:meet/from`, before the raw handle ever sees it; the second\n    25\t   refuses an append! past the bound with `:dao.stream/refused`, a\n    26\t   present answer, never silence (section 4, Bounded meeting work).\n    27\t   `meeting` composes M's own state; `step!` drains one pass of\n    28\t   `:meet-requests` and answers on `:meet-board`, publishing the\n    29\t   bound's own latest decision for the gate to read. `reclaim-fn`\n    30\t   is the idempotent reclaim procedure a composition hands\n    31\t   `dao.lease/make-judge` for the relay-pair subject this namespace\n    32\t   grants.\"\n    33\t  (:require [dao.lease :as lease]\n    34\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n    35\t            [dao.stream.middleware :as middleware]))\n    36\t\n    37\t\n    38\t;; =============================================================================\n    39\t;; The two middlewares meet-requests wraps\n    40\t;; =============================================================================\n    41\t\n    42\t(defn reflexive-tag\n    43\t  \"Middleware: an append! to meet-requests is stamped, before the raw\n    44\t   handle ever sees it, with `:meet/from` naming the channel\n    45\t   attachment identity it arrived on -- for UDP the reflexive address,\n    46\t   for any other channel whatever attachment identity the composition\n    47\t   wires. A payload's own claim about its address is never trusted:\n    48\t   the mirror step's own channel context is the source of this key,\n    49\t   never the value the asker sent.\"\n    50\t  []\n    51\t  {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n    52\t   (fn [ctx req]\n    53\t     (if (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n    54\t       (update req :dao.stream.remote/args\n    55\t               (fn [[v]]\n    56\t                 [(assoc v :meet/from (:dao.stream.remote/channel ctx))]))\n    57\t       req))\n    58\t   :dao.stream.middleware/out\n    59\t   (fn [_ctx _req outcome] outcome)})\n    60\t\n    61\t\n    62\t(defn bound-gate\n    63\t  \"Middleware: `dao.stream.middleware/gate` reading `decision`, a\n    64\t   capacity-1 medium `step!` publishes `{:meet/active-pairs n\n    65\t   :meet/max-pairs m}` onto every pass. An append! is refused,\n    66\t   present and never silent, once `n` has reached `m` -- the fanout\n    67\t   and active-pair bound of section 4's Bounded meeting work. A read\n    68\t   is never gated: the board's own retention is the only bound on\n    69\t   reading it.\"\n    70\t  [decision]\n    71\t  (middleware/gate\n    72\t    {:dao.stream.middleware/decision decision\n    73\t     :dao.stream.middleware/verify\n    74\t     (fn [d _ctx req]\n    75\t       (when (and (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n    76\t                  (number? (:meet/max-pairs d))\n    77\t                  (>= (:meet/active-pairs d 0) (:meet/max-pairs d)))\n    78\t         :dao.stream.remote-meet/past-bound))}))\n    79\t\n    80\t\n    81\t(defn entries\n    82\t  \"M's own table entries for the meeting board: `:meet-requests`,\n    83\t   `#{:writer}`, wrapped with `reflexive-tag` then `bound-gate`\n    84\t   (outermost first, so the tag runs before the gate reads the tagged\n    85\t   request -- the gate's own verify never needs the tag, but a future\n    86\t   verify might, and the position rule lets either order run; this\n    87\t   one keeps the wire-visible transform first); `:meet-board`,\n    88\t   `#{:reader}`, unwrapped. Returns `{:meet-requests entry :meet-board\n    89\t   entry}` for a table this namespace's caller merges with whatever\n    90\t   else it serves.\"\n    91\t  [{:keys [requests board decision]}]\n    92\t  {:meet-requests {:handle (middleware/wrap\n    93\t                             requests\n    94\t                             [(reflexive-tag) (bound-gate decision)])\n    95\t                   :surface #{:writer}}\n    96\t   :meet-board {:handle board :surface #{:reader}}})\n    97\t\n    98\t\n    99\t;; =============================================================================\n   100\t;; M's own state and interpreter\n   101\t;; =============================================================================\n   102\t\n   103\t(defn meeting\n   104\t  \"M's own state for the meeting board's interpreter (never the\n   105\t   mirror's own table entries, which read and write the same raw\n   106\t   `requests`/`board`/`table` handles by the composition's separate\n   107\t   wiring through `entries`). `capacity` sizes every relay ring buffer\n   108\t   this namespace creates; `max-pairs` is the bound `bound-gate`\n   109\t   enforces once `step!` has published it; `judge-atom` is the\n   110\t   composition's own `dao.lease/make-judge` state, `duration` the\n   111\t   lease this namespace grants every relay pair; `ring!` is `(fn\n   112\t   [capacity] -> handle)`, the composition's own ring buffer\n   113\t   constructor (`dao.stream.ringbuffer/create!`'s own handle, or a\n   114\t   test double).\"\n   115\t  [{:keys [requests board table capacity max-pairs decision judge-atom\n   116\t           duration ring! self]}]\n   117\t  (atom {:requests requests\n   118\t         :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor\n   119\t                            (stream/cursor requests stream/anchor-oldest))\n   120\t         :board board\n   121\t         :table table\n   122\t         :capacity capacity\n   123\t         :max-pairs max-pairs\n   124\t         :active-pairs 0\n   125\t         :decision decision\n   126\t         :judge-atom judge-atom\n   127\t         :duration duration\n   128\t         :ring! ring!\n   129\t         :self self\n   130\t         :next-id 0}))\n   131\t\n   132\t\n   133\t(defn active-pairs\n   134\t  \"The meeting's own count of live relay pairs -- reclaim-fn's own\n   135\t   bookkeeping, read here for tests and diagnostics.\"\n   136\t  [m]\n   137\t  (:active-pairs @m))\n   138\t\n   139\t\n   140\t(defn- mint-id!\n   141\t  [m prefix]\n   142\t  (let [n (:next-id @m)]\n   143\t    (swap! m update :next-id inc)\n   144\t    (str prefix \"-\" n)))\n   145\t\n   146\t\n   147\t(defn reclaim-fn\n   148\t  \"The idempotent reclaim procedure for a relay pair's lease: `subject`\n   149\t   is `[in-id out-id]`, this namespace's own grant shape. Removes both\n   150\t   identities from the table -- absent already, a no-op, so a repeated\n   151\t   call (the judge re-reaches a still-pending lease every pass) stays\n   152\t   idempotent -- and decrements the meeting's own active-pairs count\n   153\t   exactly once, guarded on the table still holding the subject. Hand\n   154\t   this to `dao.lease/make-judge`'s `:reclaim`; this namespace never\n   155\t   drives the judge itself.\"\n   156\t  [m]\n   157\t  (fn [subject]\n   158\t    (let [[in-id out-id] subject\n   159\t          table (:table @m)\n   160\t          had? (contains? @table in-id)]\n   161\t      (swap! table dissoc in-id out-id)\n   162\t      (when had? (swap! m update :active-pairs dec))\n   163\t      true)))\n   164\t\n   165\t\n   166\t(defn- remote-descriptor\n   167\t  [channel-id identity]\n   168\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/remote\n   169\t   :dao.stream/identity identity\n   170\t   :dao.stream/channel {:dao.stream/type :dao.stream.remote-meet/served\n   171\t                        :dao.stream/identity channel-id}})\n   172\t\n   173\t\n   174\t(defn- grant-pair!\n   175\t  \"Create one relay pair: two fresh ring buffers, entered in the\n   176\t   table under a fresh id pair, both surfaces declared #{:reader\n   177\t   :writer} -- the two holders tell the buffers apart by which\n   178\t   descriptor names which `in`/`out`, not by a surface difference at\n   179\t   M, which runs nothing but mirror steps over them and never reads\n   180\t   the values inside. Grants a lease over the pair's own two\n   181\t   identities as one subject, the requesting peer the holder. Returns\n   182\t   the asker's own pair descriptor's two remote descriptors.\"\n   183\t  [m holder]\n   184\t  (let [{:keys [table capacity ring! judge-atom duration]} @m\n   185\t        pair-id (mint-id! m \"pair\")\n   186\t        in-id (str pair-id \"-in\")\n   187\t        out-id (str pair-id \"-out\")]\n   188\t    (swap! table assoc\n   189\t           in-id {:handle (ring! capacity) :surface #{:reader :writer}}\n   190\t           out-id {:handle (ring! capacity) :surface #{:reader :writer}})\n   191\t    (swap! m update :active-pairs inc)\n   192\t    (swap! judge-atom lease/author-grant\n   193\t           (lease/grant pair-id [in-id out-id] holder duration))\n   194\t    {:pair-id pair-id\n   195\t     :in (remote-descriptor pair-id in-id)\n   196\t     :out (remote-descriptor pair-id out-id)}))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t(defn- handle-request!\n   200\t  [m v]\n   201\t  (cond\n   202\t    (contains? v :meet/here)\n   203\t    (stream/append! (:board @m)\n   204\t                    {:meet/seen (:meet/here v)\n   205\t                     :meet/reflexive (:meet/from v)\n   206\t                     :dao.lease/lease (mint-id! m \"reg\")})\n   207\t\n   208\t    (contains? v :meet/pair)\n   209\t    (let [holder (or (:meet/from v) (:meet/pair v))\n   210\t          {:keys [pair-id in out]} (grant-pair! m holder)]\n   211\t      (stream/append! (:board @m)\n   212\t                      {:meet/pair-for (:meet/pair v)\n   213\t                       :meet/asker (:meet/from v)\n   214\t                       :dao.lease/lease pair-id\n   215\t                       :dao.stream.remote/in in\n   216\t                       :dao.stream.remote/out out}))\n   217\t\n   218\t    :else nil))\n   219\t\n   220\t\n   221\t(defn step!\n   222\t  \"One pass of M's interpreter: publish the bound's current decision\n   223\t   for `bound-gate` to read next, then drain `:meet-requests` to\n   224\t   blocked, answering each `:meet/here` or `:meet/pair` fact on\n   225\t   `:meet-board`; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery cursor, the\n   226\t   lost asks lost. Returns `m`.\"\n   227\t  [m]\n   228\t  (let [{:keys [active-pairs max-pairs decision]} @m]\n   229\t    (stream/append! decision {:meet/active-pairs active-pairs\n   230\t                              :meet/max-pairs max-pairs}))\n   231\t  (loop []\n   232\t    (let [cursor (:requests-cursor @m)\n   233\t          r (stream/next (:requests @m) cursor)]\n   234\t      (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   235\t        :dao.stream/ok\n   236\t        (do (swap! m assoc :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   237\t            (handle-request! m (:dao.stream/value r))\n   238\t            (recur))\n   239\t\n   240\t        :dao.stream/gap\n   241\t        (do (swap! m assoc :requests-cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r))\n   242\t            (recur))\n   243\t\n   244\t        nil)))\n   245\t  m)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
