{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_18","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/cljc/dao/stream/middleware.cljc | sed -n '1,260p'\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t(ns dao.stream.middleware\n     2\t  \"DaoStream middleware: a handle-level adapter value, one `in` transform\n     3\t   over the operation map and one `out` transform over the outcome map\n     4\t   (docs/design/dao.stream.middleware.md).\n     5\t\n     6\t   A middleware is a value, never a callback: every transform here is\n     7\t   called downward by the caller and returns at once. `wrap` composes a\n     8\t   chain over a handle; `apply-request` is the one place an operation map\n     9\t   becomes a protocol call; `gate` and `present` are the two generic\n    10\t   middlewares; `encryption` and `metering` are the spec's exemplars;\n    11\t   `channel-allow-list` is the trivial policy this repository ships with.\n    12\t\n    13\t   The position rule is structural, not a convention: `wrap` validates\n    14\t   every `out` result against the permitted changes and raises on a\n    15\t   violation, so a filter cannot be expressed. Each transform is still\n    16\t   total, returns at once, never loops, retries, waits or touches the\n    17\t   inner handle, and maps inner position p to outer position p.\"\n    18\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]))\n    19\t\n    20\t\n    21\t;; =============================================================================\n    22\t;; The one dispatch point\n    23\t;; =============================================================================\n    24\t\n    25\t(defn- dispatch\n    26\t  \"Apply one operation map to a plain handle: the place an operation map\n    27\t   becomes a protocol call. An op outside the middleware vocabulary\n    28\t   (cursor, next, append!) is a defect in the host's own assembly -- the\n    29\t   mirror validates ops before this -- so it throws, per the contract's\n    30\t   reservation of exceptions (dao.stream.md, Result Convention).\"\n    31\t  [h req]\n    32\t  (let [[arg] (:dao.stream.remote/args req)]\n    33\t    (case (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n    34\t      :dao.stream/cursor (stream/cursor h arg)\n    35\t      :dao.stream/next (stream/next h arg)\n    36\t      :dao.stream/append! (stream/append! h arg)\n    37\t      (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.middleware: unknown operation\"\n    38\t                      {:op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)})))))\n    39\t\n    40\t\n    41\t(defprotocol IMiddlewareHandle\n    42\t  \"Internal seam of this namespace: the handle `wrap` returns answers one\n    43\t   whole chain pass under a caller-supplied context. `apply-request` uses\n    44\t   it so a composition (the mirror step of dao.stream.remote.md) can run\n    45\t   a table entry's middleware with its own context, exactly as the\n    46\t   wrapped handle's protocol methods run it with the local caller's {}.\n    47\t   Call `apply-request`, never this.\"\n    48\t\n    49\t  (operate-through\n    50\t    [handle ctx req]\n    51\t    \"Run the wrapped chain for operation map `req` under `ctx`.\"))\n    52\t\n    53\t\n    54\t(defn apply-request\n    55\t  \"Applies one operation map to a handle: `(apply-request h ctx req) ->\n    56\t   outcome`. On a plain handle this is the protocol call and `ctx` is\n    57\t   unused. On a handle `wrap` returned, this is the whole chain pass\n    58\t   under `ctx`: the entry point the mirror step composes with a channel\n    59\t   context. Extra qualified keys on `req` pass through untouched.\"\n    60\t  [h ctx req]\n    61\t  (if (satisfies? IMiddlewareHandle h)\n    62\t    (operate-through h ctx req)\n    63\t    (dispatch h req)))\n    64\t\n    65\t\n    66\t;; =============================================================================\n    67\t;; wrap\n    68\t;; =============================================================================\n    69\t\n    70\t(def ^:private position-keys\n    71\t  \"The outcome keys an `out` result may never change: the outcome kind,\n    72\t   the stream identity, and every key naming the operation, the request\n    73\t   id or a position -- a cursor, an anchor or a gap recovery cursor.\n    74\t   Adding any of these where the outcome had none is a change too.\"\n    75\t  [:dao.stream/outcome\n    76\t   :dao.stream/cursor\n    77\t   :dao.stream/anchor\n    78\t   :dao.stream/identity\n    79\t   :dao.stream.remote/op\n    80\t   :dao.stream.remote/id])\n    81\t\n    82\t\n    83\t(defn- position-preserving?\n    84\t  \"True when `result`, the outcome an `out` transform returns for the\n    85\t   `outcome` it received, makes none of the changes the position rule\n    86\t   forbids: no key of the outcome is dropped, the outcome kind, the\n    87\t   identity, the operation, the request id and every cursor, anchor and\n    88\t   gap recovery cursor are unchanged, and -- except for `next`'s\n    89\t   :dao.stream/value on :dao.stream/ok, the one replacement a value\n    90\t   transform owns -- the value is unchanged. Open keys may be added.\n    91\t   Structural checks over the two outcome maps only, never a walk over\n    92\t   elements.\"\n    93\t  [req outcome result]\n    94\t  (and (map? result)\n    95\t       (every? #(contains? result %) (keys outcome))\n    96\t       (every? (fn [k]\n    97\t                 (and (= (contains? outcome k) (contains? result k))\n    98\t                      (= (get outcome k) (get result k))))\n    99\t               position-keys)\n   100\t       (let [value-allowed? (and (= :dao.stream/next\n   101\t                                    (:dao.stream.remote/op req))\n   102\t                                 (= :dao.stream/ok\n   103\t                                    (:dao.stream/outcome result)))]\n   104\t         (or value-allowed?\n   105\t             (and (= (contains? outcome :dao.stream/value)\n   106\t                     (contains? result :dao.stream/value))\n   107\t                  (= (get outcome :dao.stream/value)\n   108\t                     (get result :dao.stream/value)))))))\n   109\t\n   110\t\n   111\t(defn- run-outs\n   112\t  \"Run every `out` transform from the innermost outward over `outcome`,\n   113\t   for the middlewares at chain indices below `upto`. Each result is\n   114\t   validated against the position rule: an `out` that changes anything\n   115\t   beyond the permitted replacements is a defect in the host's own\n   116\t   assembly of the chain and raises, per the contract's reservation of\n   117\t   exceptions (dao.stream.md, Result Convention) -- a filter is then\n   118\t   impossible, not merely discouraged.\"\n   119\t  [chain ctx req outcome upto]\n   120\t  (reduce\n   121\t    (fn [out i]\n   122\t      (let [result ((:dao.stream.middleware/out (nth chain i))\n   123\t                    ctx req out)]\n   124\t        (if (position-preserving? req out result)\n   125\t          result\n   126\t          (throw (ex-info \"dao.stream.middleware: out broke the position rule\"\n   127\t                          {:middleware i\n   128\t                           :op (:dao.stream.remote/op req)\n   129\t                           :received out\n   130\t                           :returned result})))))\n   131\t    outcome\n   132\t    (range (dec upto) -1 -1)))\n   133\t\n   134\t\n   135\t(defn- operate\n   136\t  \"One pass of `chain` over `req` under `ctx`: every `in` from the\n   137\t   outermost inward, the final request applied to `h` with\n   138\t   `apply-request` (which recurses into an inner wrapped handle, so\n   139\t   `ctx` carries through nesting), every `out` from the innermost\n   140\t   outward. An `in` answering an outcome map short-circuits: the inner\n   141\t   handle is not consulted and only the middlewares outside it\n   142\t   transform the outcome.\"\n   143\t  [h chain ctx req]\n   144\t  (loop [i 0, req req]\n   145\t    (if (= i (count chain))\n   146\t      (run-outs chain ctx req (apply-request h ctx req) (count chain))\n   147\t      (let [res ((:dao.stream.middleware/in (nth chain i)) ctx req)]\n   148\t        (if (stream/outcome-map? res)\n   149\t          (run-outs chain ctx req res i)\n   150\t          (recur (inc i) res))))))\n   151\t\n   152\t\n   153\t(defn- instantiated\n   154\t  \"Instantiate one middleware of a chain at wrap: when its definition\n   155\t   declares a `:dao.stream.middleware/state` constructor, `wrap` calls\n   156\t   it once, here, and specializes the definition's transforms to the\n   157\t   state minted. The state is therefore state of the wrapped handle --\n   158\t   one definition wrapped over two handles holds two states, each\n   159\t   minted by its own wrap (dao.stream.middleware.md, gate). A\n   160\t   definition that declares no constructor wraps as it is.\"\n   161\t  [mw]\n   162\t  (if-some [make (:dao.stream.middleware/state mw)]\n   163\t    (let [s (make)]\n   164\t      {:dao.stream.middleware/in\n   165\t       (fn [ctx req] ((:dao.stream.middleware/in mw) s ctx req))\n   166\t       :dao.stream.middleware/out\n   167\t       (fn [ctx req out] ((:dao.stream.middleware/out mw) s ctx req out))})\n   168\t    mw))\n   169\t\n   170\t\n   171\t(defn wrap\n   172\t  \"Compose `chain`, a vector of middleware values applied outermost\n   173\t   first, over handle `h`. The returned handle implements exactly the\n   174\t   protocols `h` implements -- descriptor, which every handle carries,\n   175\t   plus its reader, writer and closable surfaces. On each protocol call\n   176\t   it builds the operation map, runs every `in` outermost inward,\n   177\t   applies the result to `h` with `apply-request` under the local\n   178\t   caller's {} context, and runs every `out` innermost outward, each\n   179\t   `out` result validated against the position rule -- a result beyond\n   180\t   the permitted changes raises, so a filter cannot hide in a chain.\n   181\t   `wrap` also mints each middleware definition's declared state once,\n   182\t   here, so that state belongs to this wrapped handle. `descriptor` and\n   183\t   `close!` delegate to `h` unchanged: no middleware sees them. The\n   184\t   surface branches below are plain reify forms, one per combination,\n   185\t   because a handle implements its surface and no other.\"\n   186\t  [h chain]\n   187\t  (let [chain (mapv instantiated chain)\n   188\t        flow (fn [ctx req] (operate h chain ctx req))\n   189\t        r? (stream/reader? h)\n   190\t        w? (stream/writer? h)\n   191\t        c? (stream/closable? h)]\n   192\t    (cond\n   193\t      (and r? w? c?)\n   194\t      (reify\n   195\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   196\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   197\t\n   198\t\n   199\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   200\t\n   201\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   202\t\n   203\t\n   204\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   205\t\n   206\t        (cursor\n   207\t          [_ anchor]\n   208\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   209\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   210\t\n   211\t        (next\n   212\t          [_ c]\n   213\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   214\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   215\t\n   216\t\n   217\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   218\t\n   219\t        (append!\n   220\t          [_ v]\n   221\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   222\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]}))\n   223\t\n   224\t\n   225\t        stream/IDaoStreamClosable\n   226\t\n   227\t        (close! [_] (stream/close! h)))\n   228\t\n   229\t      (and r? w?)\n   230\t      (reify\n   231\t        IMiddlewareHandle\n   232\t        (operate-through [_ ctx req] (flow ctx req))\n   233\t\n   234\t\n   235\t        stream/IDaoStreamDescriptor\n   236\t\n   237\t        (descriptor [_] (stream/descriptor h))\n   238\t\n   239\t\n   240\t        stream/IDaoStreamReader\n   241\t\n   242\t        (cursor\n   243\t          [_ anchor]\n   244\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/cursor\n   245\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [anchor]}))\n   246\t\n   247\t        (next\n   248\t          [_ c]\n   249\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/next\n   250\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [c]}))\n   251\t\n   252\t\n   253\t        stream/IDaoStreamWriter\n   254\t\n   255\t        (append!\n   256\t          [_ v]\n   257\t          (flow {} {:dao.stream.remote/op :dao.stream/append!\n   258\t                    :dao.stream.remote/args [v]})))\n   259\t\n   260\t      (and r? c?)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
