nel, its id asker-minted; a next\n282:  \"Append one request map to the channel writer and register it as\n402:  \"Consume one value read off the channel. A well-formed answer whose\n424:                          (= :dao.stream/append! op))\n434:            (= :dao.stream/append! op)\n443:(defn- channel-loss!\n444:  \"The channel reader answered end: the channel is gone. The link\n450:    (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n455:  (swap! link assoc :outstanding {} :channel-gone? true))\n468:  \"Read the link's channel reader to blocked, filing each answer: the\n470:   end is the channel's loss; a gap adopts the reader's own recovery\n477:  (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n490:          :dao.stream/end (channel-loss! link)\n510:   channel loss.\"\n597:          (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n600:          (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n624:          (when-not (:channel-gone? @link)\n627:          (translated :dao.stream.remote/channel-gone)))))\n631:  \"The append! operation: send the request and return the channel\n644:      (surface-lacks? refl :dao.stream/append!)\n647:      (let [req (wire-request link refl :dao.stream/append! [v])\n674:          (when (= :dao.stream/append! (:dao.stream.remote/op (:req entry)))\n724:  \"A remote descriptor names a stream and a channel: the generic\n725:   envelope rules, the :dao.stream/remote type, and a channel\n731:       (contains? d :dao.stream/channel)))\n739:   :dao.stream.remote/channels maps each channel descriptor this peer\n741:   one process today, the ws, udp and pair channels of section 3\n744:   resend-after k, unbounded on an ordered reliable channel and small\n746:   next request. One link is kept per channel descriptor, shared by\n747:   every reflection through that channel. attach! answers ok at once\n755:  (let [channels (:dao.stream.remote/channels opts)\n763:        (let [cd (:dao.stream/channel descriptor)]\n764:          (if-not (contains? channels cd