{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/design/dao.lease.md | sed -n '230,305p'\"","aggregated_output":"   230\tfrom the resource.\n   231\t\n   232\t## Composition duties\n   233\t\n   234\tA composition that grants leases owes all of the following.\n   235\t\n   236\t- **A judging interpreter, and a runtime driving it at a declared cadence** —\n   237\t  the maximum interval between *completed* passes.\n   238\t- **A tick stream** for the judge, and one for every holder.\n   239\t- **A tolerance** supplied to the judge, possibly zero.\n   240\t- **An attribution resolver** for the judge and for every holder observing a\n   241\t  grant — its own answer to who authored a fact, by per-author media, an\n   242\t  envelope key, or a transport's attachment identity, since DaoStream supplies\n   243\t  none. One handed no resolver, or one incompatible with its medium, is refused\n   244\t  at assembly.\n   245\t- **A reclaim procedure per subject**, idempotent, reporting success.\n   246\t- **A stream the grantor writes grants and `:lapsed` to**, and the medium each\n   247\t  recipient reads its carried facts from.\n   248\t- **Media that either retain without eviction or declare evict-oldest**,\n   249\t  refused at assembly otherwise.\n   250\t- **For durable resources, three things this vocabulary does not supply**: a\n   251\t  judge whose durability matches the resource, a rule for which incarnation may\n   252\t  reclaim, and fencing from the resource. A composition that has not settled\n   253\t  all three keeps its leases process-scoped.\n   254\t\n   255\t## Sizing\n   256\t\n   257\tStated as relations; the values belong to compositions.\n   258\t\n   259\t- The granted duration exceeds twice the holder's renewal interval.\n   260\t- The judge's tolerance covers expected flight time and the rate skew between\n   261\t  its tick stream and the holder's.\n   262\t- A medium's retention window exceeds the judge's lag — cadence plus drain time.\n   263\t- A cap below the duration is permitted, and tenure then ends at the cap.\n   264\t- The holder's renewal interval plus one period of its tick stream is\n   265\t  strictly below half the granted duration: a renewal lands at the first\n   266\t  reading at or past the interval, up to one period late, so the\n   267\t  before-half guarantee is bought against interval plus period.\n   268\t\n   269\t## Limits\n   270\t\n   271\t- **A false lapse is possible.** Delay errs against the holder while a renewal\n   272\t  is unobserved and for it once observed, so a late-observed renewal from a\n   273\t  dead holder buys a fresh duration, and continuity is lost when none is\n   274\t  observed before a completed pass finds the interval past duration plus\n   275\t  tolerance. Partition length alone decides neither.\n   276\t- **`:dao.lease/max` binds within one ledger lifetime.**\n   277\t- **A medium that gaps more often than one duration** never completes an\n   278\t  observation window and leaks continuously while every component reports\n   279\t  healthy; per-attachment media are the isolation.\n   280\t- **Reclamation is bounded by** duration plus tolerance plus cadence plus the\n   281\t  reclaim's own cost, given an uninterrupted observation window.\n   282\t\n   283\t## Carriage\n   284\t\n   285\tProposals, grants, refusals, releases and renewals cross a boundary as ordinary\n   286\tpayload, carried by the composition to the medium the recipient reads. Carriage\n   287\tis delivery, not a second authoring.\n   288\t\n   289\t`:lapsed` does not cross; it is the grantor's record on the grantor's stream. A\n   290\tremote holder learns of a reclaim by observing it — for a served connection, an\n   291\tordinary `:ws/closed`; for a stream served under `dao.stream.remote.md`, the\n   292\t`not-found` protocol error its mirror answers for the reclaimed identity. A remote holder that\n   293\treads the grantor's stream through a served handle is observing the grantor's\n   294\trecord, not receiving carriage. No close code is assigned here; distinguishing\n   295\treclaim on the wire belongs to `dao.stream.ws.md`'s deferred close-code design.\n   296\t\n   297\t## Out of scope\n   298\t\n   299\t- **Delegated renewal.** A renewal is evidence about its author.\n   300\t- **Transfer of a lease between holders.**\n   301\t- **Who may be granted anything at all**, and **what is leasable** — this\n   302\t  contract gates nothing, and the domain decides. `dao.stream.remote.md`\n   303\t  names two subjects: a stream entry served for a remote party, and a relay\n   304\t  pair on a meeting peer.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
