ce when it has no cursor,\n   403\t   then calls `next` on the medium once, plus the one recovery re-read\n   404\t   after a gap; when the medium answers end the gate becomes ended and\n   405\t   reads no more. `verify` is `(fn [decision ctx req] -> nil |\n   406\t   reason)`, the adapter contract of dao.shibi.md: nil passes the\n   407\t   request through; a reason short-circuits with :dao.stream/refused.\n   408\t   Serialize calls on one wrapped handle; the gate has no queue, lock\n   409\t   or wait.\"\n   410\t  [opts]\n   411\t  (let [verify (:dao.stream.middleware/verify opts)\n   412\t        decision (:dao.stream.middleware/decision opts)\n   413\t        blank {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? false}\n   414\t        mint!\n   415\t        (fn []\n   416\t          (let [r (stream/cursor decision stream/anchor-oldest)]\n   417\t            (when (= :dao.stream/ok (:dao.stream/outcome r))\n   418\t              (:dao.stream/cursor r))))\n   419\t\n   420\t        store! (fn [state s] (vreset! state s) s)\n   421\t\n   422\t        absorb\n   423\t        (fn [s r]\n   424\t          (case (:dao.stream/outcome r)\n   425\t            :dao.stream/ok\n   426\t            {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r) :value? true\n   427\t             :value (:dao.stream/value r) :ended? false}\n   428\t\n   429\t            :dao.stream/blocked s\n   430\t\n   431\t            :dao.stream/end\n   432\t            {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   433\t\n   434\t            :dao.stream/gap\n   435\t            ;; One recovery re-read; never a third read this operation.\n   436\t            (let [rec (:dao.stream/cursor r)\n   437\t                  r2 (stream/next decision rec)]\n   438\t              (case (:dao.stream/outcome r2)\n   439\t                :dao.stream/ok\n   440\t                {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r2) :value? true\n   441\t                 :value (:dao.stream/value r2) :ended? false}\n   442\t\n   443\t                :dao.stream/blocked\n   444\t                {:cursor rec :value? false :value nil :ended? false}\n   445\t\n   446\t                :dao.stream/end\n   447\t                {:cursor nil :value? false :value nil :ended? true}\n   448\t\n   449\t                ;; A recovery gap adopts the recovery cursor and stays\n   450\t                ;; without a value.\n   451\t                :dao.stream/gap\n   452\t                {:cursor (:dao.stream/cursor r2) :value? false\n   453\t                 :value nil :ended? false}\n   454\t\n   455\t                ;; Any other recovery outcome clears cursor and value;\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
